# Practical 4: Connecting TikTok to PostgreSQL with Prisma ORM


## What I Built

For this practical I built the backend server for a TikTok clone application. I set up a REST API using Express.js, connected it to a PostgreSQL database using Prisma ORM, and implemented JWT-based authentication with bcrypt password hashing. The server handles everything — user registration and login, video uploads, likes, comments, and follow relationships — and stores all of it persistently in a real database.

---

## Tech Stack

| Tool | Purpose |
|---|---|
| Node.js + Express.js | Web server and REST API |
| PostgreSQL | Relational database |
| Prisma ORM v7 | Database schema, migrations, and queries |
| bcrypt | Password hashing |
| JSON Web Tokens (JWT) | Authentication tokens |
| Multer | Handling video and image file uploads |
| dotenv | Environment variable management |
| Nodemon | Auto-restart server during development |

---

## Project Structure

```
server/
├── prisma/
│   ├── schema.prisma       # All database models and relationships
│   ├── prisma.config.ts    # Prisma v7 database connection config
│   └── seed.js             # Script to populate DB with test data
├── src/
│   ├── controllers/
│   │   ├── userController.js     # Register, login, profile, follow
│   │   ├── videoController.js    # Upload, feed, like, comments
│   │   └── commentController.js  # Like and delete comments
│   ├── middleware/
│   │   └── auth.js               # JWT verification middleware
│   ├── routes/
│   │   ├── userRoutes.js
│   │   ├── videoRoutes.js
│   │   └── commentRoutes.js
│   ├── lib/
│   │   └── prisma.js             # Shared Prisma client instance
│   └── index.js                  # Server entry point
├── uploads/                      # Stored video and thumbnail files
├── .env
└── package.json
```

---

## Database Schema

I designed the database with 6 models in Prisma:

```prisma
User       — stores account details and hashed passwords
Video      — stores video metadata and file paths
Comment    — linked to both a user and a video
VideoLike  — many-to-many between User and Video
CommentLike — many-to-many between User and Comment
Follow     — self-referential many-to-many on User
```

The `Follow` model was the trickiest to design — it needed two separate relations on the same `User` model, one for `followers` and one for `following`, which required named relation strings in Prisma.

---

## API Endpoints

### Users
| Method | Endpoint | Protected | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| POST | `/api/users/register` | No | Create new account |
| POST | `/api/users/login` | No | Login and receive JWT |
| GET | `/api/users/me` | Yes | Get logged-in user info |
| GET | `/api/users` | Yes | List all users |
| GET | `/api/users/:id` | No | Get a user's profile |
| GET | `/api/users/:id/following` | No | Get who a user follows |
| POST | `/api/users/:id/follow` | Yes | Follow or unfollow a user |

### Videos
| Method | Endpoint | Protected | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| GET | `/api/videos` | No | Get all videos (For You feed) |
| GET | `/api/videos/following` | Yes | Get feed from followed users |
| POST | `/api/videos` | Yes | Upload a new video |
| POST | `/api/videos/:id/like` | Yes | Like or unlike a video |
| GET | `/api/videos/:id/comments` | No | Get comments on a video |
| POST | `/api/videos/:id/comments` | Yes | Post a comment |
| DELETE | `/api/videos/:id` | Yes | Delete your own video |

### Comments
| Method | Endpoint | Protected | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| POST | `/api/comments/:id/like` | Yes | Like or unlike a comment |
| DELETE | `/api/comments/:id` | Yes | Delete your own comment |

---

## Setup Instructions

### 1. Install dependencies

```bash
cd server
npm install
```

### 2. Set up PostgreSQL

```sql
CREATE DATABASE tiktok_app_db;
CREATE USER tiktok_app_user WITH ENCRYPTED PASSWORD 'tiktok123';
GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES ON DATABASE tiktok_app_db TO tiktok_app_user;
ALTER USER tiktok_app_user CREATEDB;
\c tiktok_app_db
GRANT ALL ON SCHEMA public TO tiktok_app_user;
```

### 3. Create `.env` file

```env
PORT=5000
NODE_ENV=development
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://tiktok_app_user:tiktok123@localhost:5432/tiktok_app_db?schema=public"
JWT_SECRET=mysupersecretjwtkey_tiktokapp_2024
JWT_EXPIRE=30d
```

### 4. Run migration

```bash
npx prisma migrate dev --name init
```

### 5. Seed the database

```bash
npm run seed
```

This creates 10 users, 50 videos, 200+ comments, likes, and follow relationships.

### 6. Start the server

```bash
npm run dev
```

Server runs at `http://localhost:5000`

### Test it works

Open `http://localhost:5000/api/health` — should return `{"status":"Server is running "}`

